solution.text:
From Newton's second law
$$
\begin{array}{l}
F=m a \\
m=1 \mathrm{kg} \\
F=1 \times a=\frac{d v}{d t}
\end{array}
$$
According to the question,
$$
F=k t=\frac{d v}{d t}
$$
$$
d v=k t \cdot d t
$$
Integration gives
$$
\begin{aligned}
v &=\frac{k t^{2}}{2}=\frac{d x}{d t} \\
x &=\frac{k t^{3}}{6}=\frac{1 \times 6 \times 6 \times 6}{6} \\
&=36 \mathrm{m}
\end{aligned}
$$
